# %% [markdown]
# # specs_novel — Phase 3: the search bake-off and cohort generation (Colab, GPU)
#
# `specs_novel/gate_report.md` → **G3**. Search design: `specs_novel/search_plan.md` **v1.1**.
# **Generated by `build/mk_novel_p0.py` — do not hand-edit.** Run
# `casmi_novel_p3_train_colab.ipynb` first; this notebook loads `_novel/p3/decoder.pt`.
#
# | leg | what |
# |---|---|
# | diagnostics | teacher-forced `dec_val` loss and token accuracy; **unconstrained** sampling → the share with the correct heavy-atom formula |
# | bake-off | arms **A** / **B** / **C** at an equal budget of `N_CANDIDATES` = 256, on a fixed **300-molecule `dec_val`** subset |
# | winner | highest median top-25 max Tanimoto under `maxmin`; ties → A, then C, then B |
# | cohorts | the winner **only**, on `pseudo_c3` (600) and `ts_dec` (155) |
#
# **Why the winner is picked on `dec_val` and not on `pseudo_c3`:** running three arms on the gate
# cohort and keeping the best would make the effective threshold far below the registered +0.10. The
# losing arms are never run on `pseudo_c3`, so none can be promoted after the fact.
#
# **G3 is decoder-only here.** No ICEBERG `sv`, no MetFrag-lite `fr`. G3's metrics are set metrics
# over 25 candidates and so are order-invariant; the rerank is a P4 ablation applied to *both* arms.
#
# **Resumable.** Candidates are flushed to Drive every 50 molecules with a `done_*.json` skip list.
# If Colab drops, re-run the notebook: it skips what is finished and carries on.
#
# Outputs to Drive `casmi_2026/_novel/p3/cands/`: `cands_*.parquet`, `funnel_*.jsonl`,
# `done_*.json`, and `p3_eval.json`. Paste the final printout back into the chat.

